easy-lyrics third-party attributions
=====================================

easy-lyrics aggregates lyrics from the sources below. Lyrics belong to
their publishers and songwriters; every API response carries `source`
and `sourceUrl` so credit travels with the data.

Lyric sources
-------------

- LRCLIB (MIT) — https://lrclib.net
  Free synced + plain lyrics API, no key required. Primary upstream
  source and seed for the community database (db-dumps).

- lyrics.ovh — https://lyrics.ovh
  Free plain-lyrics API. Used as the last-resort fallback.

- Megalobiz — https://www.megalobiz.com
  Community LRC (synced lyrics) archive. Queried live at request time.

- NetEase Cloud Music — https://music.163.com
  Search + lyric endpoints. Queried live at request time.

- Tencent QQ Music — https://y.qq.com
  Search + lyric endpoints. Queried live at request time.

- lrc.cx — https://lrc.cx
  Legacy LRC search API. Queried live at request time.

- Musixmatch — https://www.musixmatch.com
  Licensed lyrics API. Optional, only used when you provide your own
  MUSIXMATCH_TOKEN. Their terms apply.

Code & design references
------------------------

- syncedlyrics by moehmeni (MIT)
  https://github.com/moehmeni/syncedlyrics
  NetEase / Tencent-QQ search+lyric flow and LRC handling ported to
  TypeScript in lib/providers/netease.ts and lib/providers/tencent.ts.
  Original MIT license text applies to those portions.

- syncedlyrics_aio (MIT) — async Tencent provider reference.

- Lyrist by asrvd (MIT) — https://github.com/asrvd/lyrist
  API-shape inspiration for the Lyrist-compatible
  GET /api/:title/:artist endpoint.
